Vale (formerly Dynamic Island)
Third-party notices

The cleaner on the System page ("Bersihkan", mode "Pilih sendiri") uses a
list of locations that are safe to clean taken from Mole for Windows by tw93
(https://github.com/tw93/mole, branch `windows`, files `lib/clean/*.ps1`).

Only the data was taken: which folders each category cleans and their age
rules (temp and logs older than 7 days, installers in Downloads older than
30 days). The code that scans and deletes is the island's own, written in
Rust (`src/clean.rs`); no Mole code is copied or run.

The data comes from commit 500dfc4c27559afda21d4ed43620f90d30d5aa32 of that
branch (Mole for Windows 1.30.0), which was published under the MIT licence
below. Later commits of the branch (from 5b7695bb, 11 October 2026) are
licensed under the GPL-3.0; nothing from those is used.

The fonts embedded in the exe (DM Sans, DM Mono) are under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1; see assets/fonts/OFL.txt.

Every third-party component (the Rust crates with their versions and
licences, the fonts, Mole, and the services Vale talks to) is listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

